226C183-163 235-75 265 28C285 96 294 159 294 250C294 461 228 622 114 726L86 750L74 750C66 750 62 749 60 749Z\"></path></defs></svg>","mathFallback":false,"description":"JEE Main's 2021 JEE Main 2021 (Online) 20th July Morning Shift Paper's All Questions with solutions provider ExamSIDE.Com","paperTitle":"JEE Main 2021 (Online) 20th July Morning Shift","nextq":"1krq68vqf","prevq":"1krq52f6z","questions":[{"question_id":"1krq5ta5x","chapter":"practical-organic-chemistry","chapterGroup":"organic-chemistry","country":"in","difficulty":"medium","exam":"jee-main","examGroup":"jee","languages":["en"],"marks":4,"negMarks":1,"paperTitle":"JEE Main 2021 (Online) 20th July Morning Shift","permalink":"an-inorganic-compound-x-on-treatment-with-concentrated-hs-jee-main-chemistry-some-basic-concepts-of-chemistry-qnhdttfgvqnorqej","question":{"en":{"direction":null,"content":"An inorganic Compound 'X' on treatment with concentrated H<sub>2</sub>SO<sub>4</sub> produces brown fumes and gives dark brown ring with FeSO<sub>4</sub> in presence of concentrated H<sub>2</sub>SO<sub>4</sub>. Also Compound 'X' gives precipitate 'Y', when its solution in dilute HCl is treated with H<sub>2</sub>S gas. The precipitate 'Y' on treatment with concentrated HNO<sub>3</sub> followed by excess of NH<sub>4</sub>OH further gives deep blue coloured solution, Compound 'X' is :","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"Co(NO<sub>3</sub>)<sub>2</sub>"},{"identifier":"B","content":"Pb(NO<sub>2</sub>)<sub>2</sub>"},{"identifier":"C","content":"Cu(NO<sub>3</sub>)<sub>2</sub>"},{"identifier":"D","content":"Pb(NO<sub>3</sub>)<sub>2</sub>"}],"correct_options":["C"],"answer":null,"explanation":"Compound ‘X’ is copper nitrate, i.e. Cu(NO<sub>3</sub>)<sub>2</sub> is an inorganic\ncompound. On treatment with concentrated H<sub>2</sub>SO<sub>4</sub> produces brown\nfumes and gives dark brown ring with FeSO<sub>4</sub>\nin presence of\nconcentrated H<sub>2</sub>SO<sub>4</sub>. Chemical reaction is as follows\n<br><br><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1kx882tx0/2970b3cb-d909-4dc7-bc49-9d3999a425ba/d4c72b40-5e06-11ec-9b67-736776121a29/file-1kx882tx1.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1kx882tx0/2970b3cb-d909-4dc7-bc49-9d3999a425ba/d4c72b40-5e06-11ec-9b67-736776121a29/file-1kx882tx1.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"JEE Main 2021 (Online) 20th July Morning Shift Chemistry - Practical Organic Chemistry Question 87 English Explanation 1\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1kx882tx0/2970b3cb-d909-4dc7-bc49-9d3999a425ba/d4c72b40-5e06-11ec-9b67-736776121a29/file-1kx882tx1.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1kx882tx0/2970b3cb-d909-4dc7-bc49-9d3999a425ba/d4c72b40-5e06-11ec-9b67-736776121a29/file-1kx882tx1.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1kx882tx0/2970b3cb-d909-4dc7-bc49-9d3999a425ba/d4c72b40-5e06-11ec-9b67-736776121a29/file-1kx882tx1.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1kx882tx0/2970b3cb-d909-4dc7-bc49-9d3999a425ba/d4c72b40-5e06-11ec-9b67-736776121a29/file-1kx882tx1.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1kx882tx0/2970b3cb-d909-4dc7-bc49-9d3999a425ba/d4c72b40-5e06-11ec-9b67-736776121a29/file-1kx882tx1.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1kx882tx0/2970b3cb-d909-4dc7-bc49-9d3999a425ba/d4c72b40-5e06-11ec-9b67-736776121a29/file-1kx882tx1.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\">\n<br><br>Cu<sup>2+</sup>\nis a group II cation with group II reagents\n(HCl/H<sub>2</sub>S)\n, it gives black coloured precipitates. These precipitates\ngives blue colour solution on treatment with HNO<sub>3</sub>\nfollowed by\nexcess of NH<sub>4</sub>OH.\n<br><br><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1kx885zdb/1c22ec49-f45a-44d2-9147-87f806ee37fb/2c6aedf0-5e07-11ec-9b67-736776121a29/file-1kx885zdc.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1kx885zdb/1c22ec49-f45a-44d2-9147-87f806ee37fb/2c6aedf0-5e07-11ec-9b67-736776121a29/file-1kx885zdc.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width: 100%;height: auto;display: block;margin: 0 auto;max-height: 60vh\" alt=\"JEE Main 2021 (Online) 20th July Morning Shift Chemistry - Practical Organic Chemistry Question 87 English Explanation 2\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1kx885zdb/1c22ec49-f45a-44d2-9147-87f806ee37fb/2c6aedf0-5e07-11ec-9b67-736776121a29/file-1kx885zdc.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1kx885zdb/1c22ec49-f45a-44d2-9147-87f806ee37fb/2c6aedf0-5e07-11ec-9b67-736776121a29/file-1kx885zdc.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1kx885zdb/1c22ec49-f45a-44d2-9147-87f806ee37fb/2c6aedf0-5e07-11ec-9b67-736776121a29/file-1kx885zdc.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1kx885zdb/1c22ec49-f45a-44d2-9147-87f806ee37fb/2c6aedf0-5e07-11ec-9b67-736776121a29/file-1kx885zdc.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1kx885zdb/1c22ec49-f45a-44d2-9147-87f806ee37fb/2c6aedf0-5e07-11ec-9b67-736776121a29/file-1kx885zdc.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1kx885zdb/1c22ec49-f45a-44d2-9147-87f806ee37fb/2c6aedf0-5e07-11ec-9b67-736776121a29/file-1kx885zdc.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\">"},"hi":{"direction":null,"content":"एक अकार्बनिक यौगिक 'X' को सांद्र H<sub>2</sub>SO<sub>4</sub> के संस्लेषण से भूरे धुएँ उत्पन्न होते हैं और सांद्र H<sub>2</sub>SO<sub>4</sub> की उपस्थिति में FeSO<sub>4</sub> के साथ गहरा भूरा रिंग देता है। यौगिक 'X' जब पतले HCl में इसके घोल का H<sub>2</sub>S गैस के साथ उपचार किया जाता है तो अवक्षेप 'Y' देता है। अवक्षेप 'Y' का सांद्र HNO<sub>3</sub